"""Meetings M32–M43 (Weeks 12–16): the conference block closes, then Studios 11–12.

Week 12 (nb12) — the second week of the D50 **conference block**. The poster is
locked, so the whole week is spoken delivery: Monday builds the three timed
pitches (30 s ≤75 words, 90 s ≤200 words, 2 min ≤300 words) and the audience
analysis, Wednesday delivers them under typed adversarial questioning, and
Friday rehearses at the printed board and submits the go-public package (M14).

Week 13 (nb13) — the public test: Monday's dress rehearsal, the Expo on
**Tuesday, November 17** (required, graded, terminal), no class Wednesday, and
Friday is now **asynchronous** — the coded audience-data capture and the proof
of presentation. Week 14 (nb14) — the second asynchronous session (Mon Nov 23):
the captured questions are adjudicated into the CLAIM or only into its DEFENCE,
and M15 is due Sunday, November 29.

Weeks 15 and 16 are the post-conference studios, and they run in the STANDARD
frame: Monday and Wednesday teach the studio's lessons with their "It is your
turn" work, and Friday IS that studio's milestone. Week 15 (nb15) — **Studio
11, Reproduce and package**: Monday teaches replication and reproduction,
Wednesday teaches open and reusable packages AND runs the in-class package
exchange (a colleague cold-runs your capsule from your written instructions
alone while you run theirs), Friday repairs against that run and carries the
research note revised by two streams of criticism (M16) — the final milestone
of the chain. Week 16 (nb16) — **Studio 12, Release and direct the next
cycle**: Monday teaches Lessons 38–39 and Wednesday teaches Lesson 40. D54
retired the course milestone that used to close here, so Friday, December 11,
is the course-closing reflection session, collected under participation. The
Evidence Defences run inside the Wednesday peer-defence blocks of Weeks 15 and
16, so the standard frame is never broken to make room for them.

Course milestone ids under D50, with the D54 Sunday deadlines: M11 poster first
draft (Wed Nov 4, at class); M12 peer review submission (Fri Nov 6, 5:00 PM —
it must reach authors before the lock); M13 the terminal poster lock (Sun Nov 8,
11:59 PM); M14 the go-public package (Sun Nov 15); M15 the conference reflection
(Sun Nov 29); M16 Book Milestone 11 (Sun Dec 6) — the last milestone. There is
no M17.

Dataset numbers are recomputed from the shipped files: lapop_brazil.csv
(10,000 × 10) and foos_etal.csv (8,375 × 5), both from the rdss package
(Blair, Coppock & Humphreys, MIT License). RDSS chapter titles come from
`planning/RDSS_COVERAGE_MATRIX.md`; never invent a chapter. The AI tool named
in activities is the student's own AI assistant; GenAI Studio appears at its
designated role touchpoints (the Poster Critic at M11, the Reproducibility
Auditor at M16). No fabricated citations anywhere.
"""

